\label{posdistdec}

Suppose that $(M,g(t)),\ a<t<b$ is a Ricci flow of non-negative Ricci curvature
with $M$ a connected manifold.
Then for any points $x,y\in M$ the function $d_{g(t)}(x,y)$ is a non-increasing function of $t$.
\end{lemma}

\label{neckglue}
There is $0<\beta<1/2$ such that, for $\epsilon<1$, an evolving
$\beta\epsilon$-neck on $[-t_0,0]$ centered at $x$ with $R(x,0)=1$ and a
strong $\beta\epsilon/2$-neck on $(-t_1,-t_0]$ centered at the identified point
at time $-t_0$ glue to contain a strong $\epsilon$-neck centered at $(x,0)$.
\end{proposition}

\label{Restim}

There is $c>0$ such that $R(p,t)\ge c/(1-t)$ everywhere.
\end{proposition}
